    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0367" n="1045" xml:id="pg1045"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 47.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 10, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith No.
                    1, translation of a letter received from the ministers of foreign affairs,
                    informing me of the result of the investigations instituted into the recent
                    attack at the British legation, and the punishment inflicted on those judged
                    derelict of duty; and No. 2, translation of the document accompanying that
                    letter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>





